$DIR/main.p:30:6: r may have been moved at line 24, so it cannot be used here
    Res is an owner type: its values own what they hold and release it when they
    are dropped. r is moved out by the type assertion switch r.(type) at line 24
    on some paths to this point and not on others. On those paths r holds
    nothing afterwards, and the compiler cannot let a value be used where it may
    already belong to someone else.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    Use r before line 24, or give it a new value on the path that moves it:
        r = ...
    Or test the ok result of the assertion at line 24 directly: where it is
    false, r still holds its value:
        if !ok {
            // use r
        }
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3302" for a longer explanation)

