$DIR/main.p:48:3: v holds a view of r (r, line 45), which was given a new value at line 47, so v can no longer be used here
    v looks at memory that r owns, without owning it: the view was made by r at
    line 45. A view of an owner held in a local variable may be used only while
    the variable keeps the value the view was made from. At line 47 r was given
    a new value, so the view may look at memory that was released, or at a value
    that now belongs to something else.
    Go keeps memory alive for as long as any pointer refers to it. Plutonium has
    no garbage collector: an owner releases its memory when it is dropped, so a
    view must not be used after the value it looks at has gone.
    Use v before line 47, or give r its new value only after the last use of v
    Or make the view again after line 47:
        v = r
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3313" for a longer explanation)

